and the timing of notification in the same legal history.\"\n      ],\n      \"conflicts\": [],\n      \"alternatives\": []\n    },\n    \"version\": 1,\n    \"record\": {\n      \"path\": \"state.json\",\n      \"collection\": \"claims\",\n      \"match\": {\n        \"id\": \"claim-notify-correspondence\",\n        \"version\": 1\n      }\n    }\n  }\n]\npending_work [\n  {\n    \"id\": \"unit-claim-notify-correspondence\",\n    \"candidate_id\": \"aaa4b601803146088adba458a414a811\",\n    \"kind\": \"unit\",\n    \"remaining\": [\n      \"claim-notify-correspondence\"\n    ],\n    \"record\": {\n      \"path\": \"state.json\",\n      \"collection\": \"units\",\n      \"match\": {\n        \"id\": \"unit-claim-notify-correspondence\"\n      }\n    }\n  }\n]\ncurrent {\n  \"phase\": \"executed\",\n  \"operation_id\": \"2d4a747b58254dcda4dfb90d2fed0a8d\",\n  \"action\": \"obligation\"\n}\nbuild_inputs [\n  {\n    \"record\": \"build-inputs/targets/omnipaxos/assurance_generated/basis.json\",\n    \"manifest\": \"omnipaxos/Cargo.toml\",\n    \"test_target\": \"assurance_generated\",\n    \"resolved_features\": [\n      \"async_runtime\",\n      \"default\",\n      \"logging\",\n      \"macros\",\n      \"omnipaxos_macros\",\n      \"serde\",\n      \"slog\",\n      \"slog-async\",\n      \"slog-term\"\n    ],\n    \"feature_evidence\": \"metadata resolution; selected test compilation is recorded separately\",\n    \"compilations\": []\n  }\n]\nPLAN {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"description\": \"Concrete investigation of an accepted requirement; execution determines the observed result.\", \"properties\": {\"description\": {\"description\": \"This check\\u2019s discriminator, prefix, controls and observations; reference the accepted claim rather than restating it\", \"title\": \"Description\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"claim_id\": {\"title\": \"Claim Id\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"binding_ids\": {\"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"minItems\": 1, \"title\": \"Binding Ids\", \"type\": \"array\"}, \"harness\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/Harness\"}, \"monitors\": {\"items\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/EventMonitor\"}, \"minItems\": 1, \"title\": \"Monitors\", \"type\": \"array\"}, \"observable_properties\": {\"description\": \"Direct route supports event_assertion and event_implication. Correlate prerequisite fields by alias; observe prerequisites and results from the same legal history. Unsupported general temporal properties must remain an explicit limitation.\", \"items\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/ObservableProperty\"}, \"minItems\": 1, \"title\": \"Observable Properties\", \"type\": \"array\"}, \"uncertainties\": {\"default\": [], \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"title\": \"Uncertainties\", \"type\": \"array\"}}, \"required\": [\"description\", \"claim_id\", \"binding_ids\", \"harness\", \"monitors\", \"observable_properties\"], \"title\": \"DirectCheckPlan\", \"type\": \"object\"}\nDEFS dict_keys(['Comparison', 'EventMonitor', 'EventRequirement', 'Grounding', 'Harness', 'ObservableProperty'])\nComparison {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"field\": {\"title\": \"Field\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"op\": {\"default\": \"eq\", \"enum\": [\"eq\", \"ne\"], \"title\": \"Op\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"value\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"integer\"}, {\"type\": \"boolean\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null, \"title\": \"Value\"}, \"reference\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null, \"title\": \"Reference\"}}, \"required\": [\"field\"], \"title\": \"Comparison\", \"type\": \"object\"}\nEventMonitor {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"id\": {\"title\": \"Id\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"checker_id\": {\"title\": \"Checker Id\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"event\": {\"title\": \"Event\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"binding_ids\": {\"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"title\": \"Binding Ids\", \"type\": \"array\"}, \"grounding\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/Grounding\"}, \"applicability_conditions\": {\"default\": [], \"items\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/Comparison\"}, \"title\": \"Applicability Conditions\", \"type\": \"array\"}, \"admission_alias\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null, \"description\": \"Prerequisite alias identifying admitted operations whose completion must be observed; may depend on earlier prerequisites, never on the result or array order\", \"title\": \"Admission Alias\"}}, \"required\": [\"id\", \"checker_id\", \"event\", \"binding_ids\", \"grounding\"], \"title\": \"EventMonitor\", \"type\": \"object\"}\nEventRequirement {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"alias\": {\"title\": \"Alias\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"event\": {\"title\": \"Event\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"conditions\": {\"description\": \"Prerequisite conditions; alias references declare causal predecessors, list position does not\", \"items\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/Comparison\"}, \"title\": \"Conditions\", \"type\": \"array\"}}, \"required\": [\"alias\", \"event\"], \"title\": \"EventRequirement\", \"type\": \"object\"}\nGrounding {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"source_ids\": {\"description\": \"Exact IDs of acquired implementation source materials; not Behavior or Binding IDs\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"title\": \"Source Ids\", \"type\": \"array\"}, \"expectation_ids\": {\"description\": \"Exact IDs of acquired materials supporting the expectation; not invented expectation labels. Explain normative applicability in derivation.\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"title\": \"Expectation Ids\", \"type\": \"array\"}, \"binding_ids\": {\"default\": [], \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"title\": \"Binding Ids\", \"type\": \"array\"}, \"derivation\": {\"default\": \"\", \"description\": \"This component\\u2019s sourced reasoning; cite accepted IDs instead of repeating their full argument\", \"title\": \"Derivation\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"applicability\": {\"default\": \"\", \"description\": \"Conditions for this component, including any added assumptions or omitted protections\", \"title\": \"Applicability\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"unresolved\": {\"default\": [], \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"title\": \"Unresolved\", \"type\": \"array\"}, \"conflicts\": {\"default\": [], \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"title\": \"Conflicts\", \"type\": \"array\"}, \"alternatives\": {\"default\": [], \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"title\": \"Alternatives\", \"type\": \"array\"}}, \"title\": \"Grounding\", \"type\": \"object\"}\nHarness {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"execution_package\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null, \"description\": \"Optional single local Go package or Rust crate directory; the controller fixes the effective package at acceptance\", \"title\": \"Execution Package\"}, \"files\": {\"additionalProperties\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"description\": \"Additional generated files with relative destinations and fixed source text\", \"title\": \"Files\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"kind\": {\"description\": \"Harness kind advertised by the configured execution backend\", \"title\": \"Kind\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"source\": {\"description\": \"Executable experiment source, calling actual target code; no fabricated expected observations\", \"minLength\": 1, \"title\": \"Source\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"description\": {\"title\": \"Description\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"semantic_changes\": {\"description\": \"Instrumentation and adaptation differences; never alter protocol logic to create a real finding\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"title\": \"Semantic Changes\", \"type\": \"array\"}, \"prerequisites\": {\"default\": [], \"items\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/EventRequirement\"}, \"title\": \"Prerequisites\", \"type\": \"array\"}, \"legality\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/Grounding\", \"default\": {\"source_ids\": [], \"expectation_ids\": [], \"binding_ids\": [], \"derivation\": \"\", \"applicability\": \"\", \"unresolved\": [], \"conflicts\": [], \"alternatives\": []}}}, \"required\": [\"kind\", \"source\", \"description\", \"semantic_changes\"], \"title\": \"Harness\", \"type\": \"object\"}\nObservableProperty {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"checker_id\": {\"title\": \"Checker Id\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"kind\": {\"default\": \"event_assertion\", \"enum\": [\"event_assertion\", \"event_implication\"], \"title\": \"Kind\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"trigger\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/Comparison\"}, \"assertion\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/Comparison\"}, \"antecedent\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/Comparison\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"identity_fields\": {\"description\": \"Independent operation identity shared by prerequisites and result; never the value being compared or a context expected to change\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"title\": \"Identity Fields\", \"type\": \"array\"}, \"description\": {\"title\": \"Description\", \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"checker_id\", \"trigger\", \"assertion\", \"description\"], \"title\": \"ObservableProperty\", \"type\": \"object\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat ../agent-source/omnipaxos_runtime/src/lib.rs; sed -n '1,130p' ../agent-source/omnipaxos_runtime/tests/async_runtime_test.rs; cat ../agent-source/omnipaxos/src/utils/logger.rs; sed -n '1,90p' ../agent-source/omnipaxos/src/storage/mod.rs; sed -n '20,80p' ../agent-source/omnipaxos/src/messages.rs; cat ../agent-source/Cargo.toml; cat ../build-inputs/targets/omnipaxos/assurance_generated/basis.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat ../agent-source/omnipaxos_runtime/src/lib.rs; sed -n '1,130p' ../agent-source/omnipaxos_runtime/tests/async_runtime_test.rs; cat ../agent-source/omnipaxos/src/utils/logger.rs; sed -n '1,90p' ../agent-source/omnipaxos/src/storage/mod.rs; sed -n '20,80p' ../agent-source/omnipaxos/src/messages.rs; cat ../agent-source/Cargo.toml; cat ../build-inputs/targets/omnipaxos/assurance_generated/basis.json\"","aggregated_output":"//! Async runtime actor layer for OmniPaxos.\n//!\n//! The [`AsyncRuntime`] trait abstracts over the async executor so this crate can be used\n//! on top of any runtime. A ready-to-use [`TokioRuntime`] is provided behind the\n//! `tokio_runtime` feature.\n//!\n//! The main entry point is [`spawn_actor`], which takes an\n//! [`OmniPaxos`](omnipaxos::OmniPaxos) instance and returns an [`OmniPaxosHandle`]. The\n//! handle is cloneable and provides `async` methods to append entries and observe state\n//! transitions.\n//!\n//! The runtime does NOT own message transport: use [`OmniPaxosHandle::outgoing_messages`]\n//! to drain outgoing messages and [`OmniPaxosHandle::handle_incoming`] to deliver\n//! incoming ones. This keeps the crate free of I/O dependencies and lets users plug in\n//! any transport (TCP, QUIC, in-process channels, etc.).\n\n#![deny(missing_docs)]\n\nmod actor;\nmod event;\nmod handle;\nmod traits;\n\n#[cfg(feature = \"tokio_runtime\")]\nmod tokio_rt;\n\npub use event::{AppendError, OmniPaxosEvent, RuntimeProposeErr};\npub use handle::{spawn_actor, OmniPaxosHandle, RuntimeConfig};\npub use omnipaxos::messages::EntryId;\npub use traits::{ActorEntry, AsyncRuntime};\n\n#[cfg(feature = \"tokio_runtime\")]\npub use tokio_rt::TokioRuntime;\n//! Integration tests for the async runtime layer.\n//!\n//! Sets up a small in-process cluster where each node runs an OmniPaxos actor and messages\n//! are shuttled between them over in-memory channels, then exercises the async API.\n#![cfg(feature = \"tokio_runtime\")]\n\nuse std::{\n    collections::HashMap,\n    sync::{\n        atomic::{AtomicBool, Ordering},\n        Arc,\n    },\n    time::Duration,\n};\n\n#[cfg(feature = \"unicache\")]\nuse omnipaxos::unicache::UniCache;\nuse omnipaxos::{\n    messages::{sequence_paxos::PaxosMsg, Message},\n    storage::{Entry, Snapshot},\n    util::{LogEntry, NodeId},\n    ClusterConfig, OmniPaxosConfig, ProposeErr, ServerConfig,\n};\nuse omnipaxos_runtime::{\n    spawn_actor, AppendError, OmniPaxosEvent, OmniPaxosHandle, RuntimeConfig, RuntimeProposeErr,\n    TokioRuntime,\n};\nuse omnipaxos_storage::memory_storage::MemoryStorage;\nuse tokio::time::timeout;\n\n/// Minimal Entry type — avoids depending on the `macros` feature. Always derives serde\n/// traits (an unconditional dev-dependency here) rather than gating on this crate's own\n/// `serde` feature: under workspace-wide builds (`cargo check --workspace`), `omnipaxos`'s\n/// `serde` feature can be active (enabled by some other workspace member) independently of\n/// whether *this* crate's `serde` feature was requested, and `Entry::Snapshot` requires\n/// `Serialize + Deserialize` whenever the dependency's feature is on, regardless.\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, Default, PartialEq, serde::Serialize, serde::Deserialize)]\nstruct TestEntry(u64);\n\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, Default, serde::Serialize, serde::Deserialize)]\nstruct NoSnapshot;\n\nimpl Snapshot<TestEntry> for NoSnapshot {\n    fn create(_entries: &[TestEntry]) -> Self {\n        NoSnapshot\n    }\n    fn merge(&mut self, _delta: Self) {}\n    fn use_snapshots() -> bool {\n        false\n    }\n}\n\n/// No-op UniCache so `cargo test --all-features` can compile without the macros crate.\n#[cfg(feature = \"unicache\")]\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, Default, serde::Serialize, serde::Deserialize)]\nstruct NoUniCache;\n\n#[cfg(feature = \"unicache\")]\nimpl UniCache for NoUniCache {\n    type T = TestEntry;\n\n    fn new() -> Self {\n        NoUniCache\n    }\n\n    fn try_encode(&mut self, entry: &Self::T) -> <Self::T as Entry>::EncodeResult {\n        entry.clone()\n    }\n\n    fn decode(&mut self, processed: <Self::T as Entry>::EncodeResult) -> Self::T {\n        processed\n    }\n}\n\nimpl Entry for TestEntry {\n    type Snapshot = NoSnapshot;\n\n    #[cfg(feature = \"unicache\")]\n    type Encoded = ();\n    #[cfg(feature = \"unicache\")]\n    type Encodable = TestEntry;\n    #[cfg(feature = \"unicache\")]\n    type NotEncodable = ();\n    #[cfg(feature = \"unicache\")]\n    type EncodeResult = TestEntry;\n    #[cfg(feature = \"unicache\")]\n    type UniCache = NoUniCache;\n}\n\nfn build_op(\n    pid: NodeId,\n    nodes: Vec<NodeId>,\n) -> omnipaxos::OmniPaxos<TestEntry, MemoryStorage<TestEntry>> {\n    let cluster_config = ClusterConfig {\n        configuration_id: 1,\n        nodes,\n        flexible_quorum: None,\n    };\n    // `..Default::default()` is needed only when the `logging` feature adds\n    // extra fields to `ServerConfig`; clippy flags it as redundant under\n    // feature combinations where it isn't (e.g. `logging` off).\n    #[allow(clippy::needless_update)]\n    let server_config = ServerConfig {\n        pid,\n        election_tick_timeout: 3,\n        resend_message_tick_timeout: 5,\n        buffer_size: 100,\n        batch_size: 1,\n        flush_batch_tick_timeout: 100,\n        leader_priority: 0,\n        ..Default::default()\n    };\n    let cfg = OmniPaxosConfig {\n        cluster_config,\n        server_config,\n    };\n    cfg.build(MemoryStorage::default()).unwrap()\n}\n\n/// Spawn `n` nodes and wire their outgoing/incoming message streams together.\nasync fn spawn_cluster(n: NodeId) -> HashMap<NodeId, OmniPaxosHandle<TestEntry>> {\n    let nodes: Vec<NodeId> = (1..=n).collect();\n    let cfg = RuntimeConfig {\n        tick_period: Duration::from_millis(2),\n        egress_period: Duration::from_millis(1),\n        ..Default::default()\n    };\n\n    let mut handles: HashMap<NodeId, OmniPaxosHandle<TestEntry>> = HashMap::new();\n    for pid in nodes.clone() {\nuse slog::{o, Drain, Logger};\nuse std::{fs::OpenOptions, sync::Mutex};\n\n/// Creates an asynchronous logger which outputs to both the terminal and a specified file_path.\npub fn create_logger(file_path: &str) -> Logger {\n    let path = std::path::Path::new(file_path);\n    let prefix = path.parent().unwrap(); // todo change unwrap\n    std::fs::create_dir_all(prefix).unwrap(); // todo change unwrap\n\n    let file = OpenOptions::new()\n        .create(true)\n        .write(true)\n        .truncate(true)\n        .open(file_path)\n        .unwrap(); // todo change unwrap\n\n    let term_decorator = slog_term::TermDecorator::new().build();\n    let file_decorator = slog_term::PlainSyncDecorator::new(file);\n\n    let term_fuse = slog_term::FullFormat::new(term_decorator).build().fuse();\n    let file_fuse = slog_term::FullFormat::new(file_decorator).build().fuse();\n\n    let both = Mutex::new(slog::Duplicate::new(term_fuse, file_fuse)).fuse();\n    let both = slog_async::Async::new(both).build().fuse();\n    Logger::root(both, o!())\n}\npub(crate) mod internal_storage;\nmod state_cache;\n\nuse super::ballot_leader_election::Ballot;\n#[cfg(feature = \"unicache\")]\nuse crate::unicache::*;\nuse crate::ClusterConfig;\n#[cfg(feature = \"serde\")]\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\nuse std::{error::Error, fmt::Debug};\n\n/// Type of the entries stored in the log.\npub trait Entry: Clone + Debug {\n    #[cfg(not(feature = \"serde\"))]\n    /// The snapshot type for this entry type.\n    type Snapshot: Snapshot<Self>;\n\n    #[cfg(feature = \"serde\")]\n    /// The snapshot type for this entry type.\n    type Snapshot: Snapshot<Self> + Serialize + for<'a> Deserialize<'a>;\n\n    #[cfg(feature = \"unicache\")]\n    /// The encoded type of some data. If there is a cache hit in UniCache, the data will be replaced and get sent over the network as this type instead. E.g., if `u8` then the cached `Entry` (or field of it) will be sent as `u8` instead.\n    type Encoded: Encoded;\n    #[cfg(feature = \"unicache\")]\n    /// The type representing the encodable parts of an `Entry`. It can be set to `Self` if the whole `Entry` is cachable. See docs of `pre_process()` for an example of deriving `Encodable` from an `Entry`.\n    type Encodable: Encodable;\n    #[cfg(feature = \"unicache\")]\n    /// The type representing the **NOT** encodable parts of an `Entry`. Any `NotEncodable` data will be transmitted in its original form, without encoding. It can be set to `()` if the whole `Entry` is cachable. See docs of `pre_process()` for an example.\n    type NotEncodable: NotEncodable;\n\n    #[cfg(all(feature = \"unicache\", not(feature = \"serde\")))]\n    /// The type that represents if there was a cache hit or miss in UniCache.\n    type EncodeResult: Clone + Debug;\n\n    #[cfg(all(feature = \"unicache\", feature = \"serde\"))]\n    /// The type that represents the results of trying to encode i.e., if there was a cache hit or miss in UniCache.\n    type EncodeResult: Clone + Debug + Serialize + for<'a> Deserialize<'a>;\n\n    #[cfg(all(feature = \"unicache\", not(feature = \"serde\")))]\n    /// The type that represents the results of trying to encode i.e., if there was a cache hit or miss in UniCache.\n    type UniCache: UniCache<T = Self>;\n    #[cfg(all(feature = \"unicache\", feature = \"serde\"))]\n    /// The unicache type for caching popular/re-occurring fields of an entry.\n    type UniCache: UniCache<T = Self> + Serialize + for<'a> Deserialize<'a>;\n}\n\n/// A StopSign entry that marks the end of a configuration. Used for reconfiguration.\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq)]\n#[cfg_attr(feature = \"serde\", derive(Serialize, Deserialize))]\npub struct StopSign {\n    /// The new `Omnipaxos` cluster configuration\n    pub next_config: ClusterConfig,\n    /// Metadata for the reconfiguration.\n    pub metadata: Option<Vec<u8>>,\n}\n\nimpl StopSign {\n    /// Creates a [`StopSign`].\n    pub fn with(next_config: ClusterConfig, metadata: Option<Vec<u8>>) -> Self {\n        StopSign {\n            next_config,\n            metadata,\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n/// Snapshot type. A `Complete` snapshot contains all snapshotted data while `Delta` has snapshotted changes since an earlier snapshot.\n#[allow(missing_docs)]\n#[derive(Clone, Debug)]\n#[cfg_attr(feature = \"serde\", derive(Serialize, Deserialize))]\npub enum SnapshotType<T>\nwhere\n    T: Entry,\n{\n    Complete(T::Snapshot),\n    Delta(T::Snapshot),\n}\n\n/// Trait for implementing snapshot operations for log entries of type `T` in OmniPaxos.\npub trait Snapshot<T>: Clone + Debug\nwhere\n    T: Entry,\n{\n    /// Create a snapshot from the log `entries`.\n    fn create(entries: &[T]) -> Self;\n\n    /// Merge another snapshot `delta` into self.\n    fn merge(&mut self, delta: Self);\n\n    use serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\n    use std::fmt::Debug;\n\n    /// Message sent by a follower on crash-recovery or dropped messages to request its leader to re-prepare them.\n    #[derive(Copy, Clone, Debug)]\n    #[cfg_attr(feature = \"serde\", derive(Serialize, Deserialize))]\n    pub struct PrepareReq {\n        /// The current round.\n        pub n: Ballot,\n    }\n\n    /// Prepare message sent by a newly-elected leader to initiate the Prepare phase.\n    #[derive(Copy, Clone, Debug)]\n    #[cfg_attr(feature = \"serde\", derive(Serialize, Deserialize))]\n    pub struct Prepare {\n        /// The current round.\n        pub n: Ballot,\n        /// The decided index of this leader.\n        pub decided_idx: usize,\n        /// The latest round in which an entry was accepted.\n        pub n_accepted: Ballot,\n        /// The log length of this leader.\n        pub accepted_idx: usize,\n    }\n\n    /// Promise message sent by a follower in response to a [`Prepare`] sent by the leader.\n    #[derive(Clone, Debug)]\n    #[cfg_attr(feature = \"serde\", derive(Serialize, Deserialize))]\n    pub struct Promise<T>\n    where\n        T: Entry,\n    {\n        /// The current round.\n        pub n: Ballot,\n        /// The latest round in which an entry was accepted.\n        pub n_accepted: Ballot,\n        /// The decided index of this follower.\n        pub decided_idx: usize,\n        /// The log length of this follower.\n        pub accepted_idx: usize,\n        /// The log update which the leader applies to its log in order to sync\n        /// with this follower (if the follower is more up-to-date).\n        pub log_sync: Option<LogSync<T>>,\n    }\n\n    /// AcceptSync message sent by the leader to synchronize the logs of all replicas in the prepare phase.\n    #[derive(Clone, Debug)]\n    #[cfg_attr(feature = \"serde\", derive(Serialize, Deserialize))]\n    pub struct AcceptSync<T>\n    where\n        T: Entry,\n    {\n        /// The current round.\n        pub n: Ballot,\n        /// The sequence number of this message in the leader-to-follower accept sequence\n        pub seq_num: SequenceNumber,\n        /// The decided index\n        pub decided_idx: usize,\n        /// The log update which the follower applies to its log in order to sync\n        /// with the leader.\n        pub log_sync: LogSync<T>,\n[workspace]\nresolver = \"2\"\nmembers = [\n    \"omnipaxos\",\n    \"omnipaxos_storage\",\n    \"omnipaxos_macros\",\n    \"omnipaxos_runtime\",\n    \"omnipaxos_ui\",\n    \"examples/kv_store\",\n    \"examples/kv_store_async\",\n    \"examples/dashboard\",\n]\n\n[profile.release]\nlto = true\n{\n  \"snapshot_id\": \"86cf6c826e0c4ad19234d3f0b9ca1351\",\n  \"source_files\": {\n    \".gitignore\": \"8409c7441e162cb655b6af32877544b2b1240f7bdf0b1758839b035cfd5fa882\",\n    \"Cargo.toml\": \"60d6df52da137a445b9e3bf769e033d90f9210be286f5a65b015703b386768ec\",\n    \"LICENSE\": \"c71d239df91726fc519c6eb72d318ec65820627232b2f796219e87dcf35d0ab4\",\n    \"README.md\": \"11e56a09ff34ab461544976dab476bf5